{
  "_readme": "Manifest consumed by `sta demo`. Each clip ships its video, its detections and the study's own human annotation, so the demo runs with no model, no GPU and no network, and opens on finished work.",
  "source": {
    "study": "Broiler activity on a non-perforated grooved floor, Texas A&M University Poultry Science Center, 2025",
    "iacuc": "Texas A&M University IACUC protocol 2024-0108",
    "camera": "Intel RealSense D415, RGB stream, 848 x 480 at 5 fps, 2.5 m above the floor, each camera covering two pens",
    "detector": "YOLO11x fine tuned on 720 overhead frames of the same house",
    "tracker": "ByteTrack, run per pen, match 0.70 / new 0.35 / buffer 60 at 5 fps",
    "annotation": "the census annotation of the study: every detected bird in every frame carries a state assigned by a human watching that bird, not inferred from box displacement. Imported into this tool's format; segments and per-frame states carry over untouched and every derived field is recomputed by core.reconcile()",
    "selection": "chosen for a high annotated activity fraction first, then for the number of distinct individuals that move, then for a low human audited detector miss rate. The four span weeks 1 to 3 of the grow-out, two cameras and three times of day",
    "license": "CC BY 4.0, see examples/LICENSE-DATA.txt"
  },
  "project": {
    "name": "broiler activity demo",
    "playback_fps": 5,
